.Dd June 26, 2026
.Dt SLACKFETCH 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm slackfetch
.Nd minimal system information utility for Slackware
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
displays a small set of system information relevant to a
Slackware Linux system.
Only information that can be determined reliably is shown.
.Pp
Desktop environment and window manager fields are omitted
when they cannot be determined.
.Sh INSTALLATION
Local installation:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
install -m 0755 slackfetch ~/.local/bin/slackfetch
.Ed
.Pp
System-wide installation:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
install -m 0755 slackfetch /usr/bin/slackfetch
.Ed
.Sh EXAMPLES
Window manager only (dwm):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ slackfetch
     ________    r1w1s1@RachaelTyrell (ThinkPad T14 Gen 2i)
    /  ______|   os:        Slackware 15.0+
    | |______    kernel:    Linux 7.0.12 (x86_64)
    \e______  \e   libc:      glibc 2.42
     ______| |   uptime:    1 hour, 57 minutes (age 394d)
  | |________/   shell:     GNU bash 5.3.15 (tmux)
  |____________  pkgs:      1297 (63 SBo, 12 Flatpak)
                 wm:        dwm (XLibre 1.25.1)
.Ed
.Pp
Desktop environment (KDE):
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ slackfetch
     ________    r1w1s1@x220 (ThinkPad X220)
    /  ______|   os:        Slackware 15.0+
    | |______    kernel:    Linux 7.1.0 (x86_64)
    \e______  \e   libc:      glibc 2.42
     ______| |   uptime:    42 minutes (age 394d)
  | |________/   shell:     GNU bash
  |____________  pkgs:      1297 (63 SBo)
                 de:        KDE 6.4.0
                 wm:        KWin (Wayland)
.Ed
.Pp
Disable colored output:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ NO_COLOR=1 slackfetch
.Ed
.Pp
Override window manager detection:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ SLACKFETCH_WM="dwm 6.8" slackfetch
.Ed
.Pp
Override machine model:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ SLACKFETCH_MODEL="QEMU" slackfetch
.Ed
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width SLACKFETCH_MODEL
.It Ev SLACKFETCH_WM
Override window manager detection.
This is primarily intended for non-EWMH window managers such as
.Xr twm 1 ,
.Xr ctwm 1 ,
or
.Xr mwm 1 .
The value is shown verbatim.
.Pp
Example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
SLACKFETCH_WM="dwm 6.8" slackfetch
.Ed
.It Ev SLACKFETCH_MODEL
Override machine model detection.
The value is shown verbatim.
.Pp
Example:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
SLACKFETCH_MODEL="QEMU" slackfetch
.Ed
.It Ev NO_COLOR
Disable colored output according to the
.Lk https://no-color.org NO_COLOR
convention.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/slackware-version
.It Pa /etc/slackware-version
Slackware version string.
.It Pa /var/log/packages
Installed package database used for the
.Dq pkgs:
field.
.It Pa /lib64/libc.so.6 , Pa /lib/libc.so.6
glibc version used for the
.Dq libc:
field.
.It Pa /sys/devices/virtual/dmi/id/sys_vendor
Machine vendor used for model selection.
.It Pa /sys/devices/virtual/dmi/id/product_name
Machine model information when available.
.It Pa /sys/devices/virtual/dmi/id/product_version
Fallback machine model information.
.El
.Sh NOTES
Window manager detection relies on the EWMH
.Dv _NET_WM_NAME
property via
.Xr xprop 1
when running under X11.
Non-EWMH window managers may be specified using
.Ev SLACKFETCH_WM .
The
.Dq age
value is shown in the
.Dq uptime:
field based on the installation time of
.Pa aaa_base
package.
The
.Dq libc:
field is shown when glibc can be read from
.Pa /lib64/libc.so.6
or
.Pa /lib/libc.so.6 .
The
.Dq pkgs:
field is shown when
.Pa /var/log/packages
is available.
Packages ending in
.Dq _SBo
are counted as SlackBuilds.org packages.
Flatpak applications are counted when the flatpak command is installed.
.Pp
The
.Dq de:
field is shown only when
.Ev XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP
is present.
KDE and XFCE include a version when it can be read from their own tools.
The
.Dq wm:
field is shown only when a window manager can be determined.
Under Wayland,
.Nm
reports
.Dq Wayland
when
.Ev WAYLAND_DISPLAY
is present.
.Pp
To add better model detection for another machine vendor, report the output of:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
cat /sys/devices/virtual/dmi/id/sys_vendor
cat /sys/devices/virtual/dmi/id/product_name
cat /sys/devices/virtual/dmi/id/product_version
.Ed
.Pp
Also include the model name that should be displayed.
Do not send serial numbers, UUIDs, or other unique machine identifiers.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr uname 1 ,
.Xr uptime 1 ,
.Xr xprop 1
